 "granularity_rationale": "Articles and numbered paragraphs are the units an auditor tests a control against (e.g. GDPR art:32(1)); lettered points and sub-points are NOT listed, but references to them are accepted when their parent identifier is listed. A paragraph identifier is only listed where the paragraph carries an explicit number in the official text (single-paragraph articles get no paragraph identifier). Recitals are listed as recital:N because the purpose of the legislation is expressed there and regulators and courts cite them; annex:I (sectors of high criticality) and annex:II (other critical sectors) are listed because entity scope is determined by them. Annex III is only the correlation table to the repealed Directive (EU) 2016/1148 and is not listed.",
